**17. [M] [LC 1861 · Rotating the Box](https://leetcode.com/problems/rotating-the-box/){difficulty="Medium"}. A grid holds stones `#`, obstacles `*` and empty cells `.`. Rotate it $90°$ clockwise; gravity then makes every stone fall onto an obstacle, another stone, or the bottom. Return the result.**

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
After a clockwise rotation, "down" is the direction of increasing column index in the original grid. So first let the stones slide *right* in every row, then rotate. Sliding is a write pointer per row moving right to left: `w` is where the next stone lands, an obstacle at column $r$ resets it to $r - 1$, and a stone at $r$ is lifted and dropped at `w`, then `w -= 1`. Since $w \ge r$, a stone never lands on an unread stone. The rotation itself is index arithmetic: `res[j][m - 1 - i] = box[i][j]`. Time $O(mn)$.

::: {#f8fe1f01 .cell execution_count=82}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def ex17_rotate_box(box):
    box = [row[:] for row in box]
    m, n = len(box), len(box[0])
    for row in box:
        w = n - 1
        for r in range(n - 1, -1, -1):
            if row[r] == "*":
                w = r - 1                       # an obstacle starts a new segment
            elif row[r] == "#":
                row[r], row[w] = ".", "#"
                w -= 1
    return [[box[m - 1 - i][j] for i in range(m)] for j in range(n)]

def ex17_brute(box):
    box = [row[:] for row in box]
    moved = True
    while moved:                                # move stones right one cell at a time
        moved = False
        for row in box:
            for c in range(len(row) - 1):
                if row[c] == "#" and row[c + 1] == ".":
                    row[c], row[c + 1], moved = ".", "#", True
    m, n = len(box), len(box[0])
    return [[box[m - 1 - i][j] for i in range(m)] for j in range(n)]

assert ex17_rotate_box([["#", ".", "*", "."], ["#", "#", "*", "."]]) == \
    [["#", "."], ["#", "#"], ["*", "*"], [".", "."]]
for _ in range(300):
    e17 = [[random.choice("#.*.") for _ in range(random.randint(1, 5))]]
    e17 += [[random.choice("#.*.") for _ in range(len(e17[0]))] for _ in range(random.randint(0, 3))]
    assert ex17_rotate_box(e17) == ex17_brute(e17)
```
