**30. [E] [CF 1352A · Sum of Round Numbers](https://codeforces.com/problemset/problem/1352/A){rating="800"}. A number is round if all its digits except the first are zero. Write $n \le 10^4$ as a sum of as few round numbers as possible.**

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
Every non-zero digit $d$ at place $10^i$ contributes the round number $d\cdot 10^i$, and no round number can cover two non-zero digits, so the minimum is the number of non-zero digits. Walk the digits from the least significant end, as in a carry loop.

::: {#f55a4363 .cell execution_count=95}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def ex30_round(n):
    out, place = [], 1
    while n:
        if n % 10:
            out.append((n % 10) * place)
        n, place = n // 10, place * 10
    return out

assert sorted(ex30_round(5009)) == [9, 5000] and ex30_round(7) == [7] and len(ex30_round(9876)) == 4
assert all(sum(ex30_round(x)) == x and len(ex30_round(x)) == sum(c != "0" for c in str(x)) for x in range(1, 10_001))
```
:::


