**31. [M] [LC 2582 · Pass the Pillow](https://leetcode.com/problems/pass-the-pillow/){difficulty="Easy"}. People $1..n$ stand in a line, person 1 holds a pillow, and every second it moves to the next person; at either end the direction reverses. Who holds it after `time` seconds? Make it work for `time` up to $10^{18}$.**

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
A back-and-forth walk over $n$ people has period $2(n - 1)$: after that many seconds the pillow is back at person 1, moving forward. Let $r = \text{time} \bmod 2(n-1)$. For $r \le n - 1$ the pillow is going forward and is at person $1 + r$; otherwise it is coming back and is at person $2n - 1 - r$. The simulation is $O(\text{time})$, the formula $O(1)$.

::: {#8b9328ec .cell execution_count=96}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def ex31_pillow(n, time):
    r = time % (2 * (n - 1))
    return 1 + r if r <= n - 1 else 2 * n - 1 - r

def ex31_simulate(n, time):
    pos, step = 1, 1
    for _ in range(time):
        if not 1 <= pos + step <= n:
            step = -step
        pos += step
    return pos

assert ex31_pillow(4, 5) == 2 and ex31_pillow(3, 2) == 3
assert all(ex31_pillow(n, t) == ex31_simulate(n, t) for n in range(2, 8) for t in range(1, 40))
assert ex31_pillow(1000, 10**18) == ex31_pillow(1000, 10**18 % 1998)
```
:::


