**33. [E] [LC 1394 · Find Lucky Integer in an Array](https://leetcode.com/problems/find-lucky-integer-in-an-array/){difficulty="Easy"}. A value is lucky if it occurs exactly as many times as its value. Return the largest lucky value, or $-1$.**

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
Values are at most $500$: count them in an array and scan the values from the top, returning the first $v$ with `cnt[v] == v`.

::: {#3cc4cf60 .cell execution_count=98}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def ex33_lucky(a):
    cnt = [0] * 501
    for x in a:
        cnt[x] += 1
    return next((v for v in range(500, 0, -1) if cnt[v] == v), -1)

assert [ex33_lucky(t) for t in ([2, 2, 3, 4], [1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3], [2, 2, 2, 3, 3])] == [2, 3, -1]
```
