**34. [E] [LC 2006 · Count Number of Pairs With Absolute Difference K](https://leetcode.com/problems/count-number-of-pairs-with-absolute-difference-k/){difficulty="Easy"}. Count the pairs $i < j$ with $|a_i - a_j| = k$ (values $\le 100$, $k \ge 1$).**

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
A pair with values $v$ and $v + k$ is counted once whichever comes first, so the answer is $\sum_v \texttt{cnt}[v]\cdot\texttt{cnt}[v + k]$: pairs by value (@sec-arr-p5), $O(n + V)$ instead of $O(n^2)$.

::: {#7191e52e .cell execution_count=99}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def ex34_pairs(a, k):
    cnt = [0] * (101 + k)
    for x in a:
        cnt[x] += 1
    return sum(cnt[v] * cnt[v + k] for v in range(101))

assert ex34_pairs([1, 2, 2, 1], 1) == 4 and ex34_pairs([1, 3], 3) == 0 and ex34_pairs([3, 2, 1, 5, 4], 2) == 3
for _ in range(500):
    e34, e34_k = [random.randint(1, 6) for _ in range(random.randint(1, 9))], random.randint(1, 4)
    assert ex34_pairs(e34, e34_k) == sum(abs(x - y) == e34_k for x, y in combinations(e34, 2))
```
