**39. [H] [LC 238 · Product of Array Except Self](https://leetcode.com/problems/product-of-array-except-self/){difficulty="Medium"}. Return, for every $i$, the product of all other elements, in $O(n)$ without division, then with $O(1)$ extra space beyond the output.**

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
Each position needs its left side *and* its right side (@sec-arr-scan), so it is a prefix product times a suffix product. Write the prefix products into the output array in a forward pass; then a backward pass multiplies in a *running* suffix product, one variable instead of a second array. Division would fail on zeros.

::: {#43cc4591 .cell execution_count=104}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def ex39_except_self(a):
    n = len(a)
    out = [1] * n
    for i in range(1, n):
        out[i] = out[i - 1] * a[i - 1]            # product of a[0:i]
    suffix = 1
    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):
        out[i] *= suffix                          # times product of a[i+1:n]
        suffix *= a[i]
    return out

assert ex39_except_self([1, 2, 3, 4]) == [24, 12, 8, 6] and ex39_except_self([-1, 1, 0, -3, 3]) == [0, 0, 9, 0, 0]
for _ in range(500):
    e39 = [random.randint(-3, 3) for _ in range(random.randint(2, 7))]
    assert ex39_except_self(e39) == [math.prod(e39[:i] + e39[i + 1:]) for i in range(len(e39))]
```
:::


